Syntax: cast 'cloud of concealment'

Cloud of Concealment summons a thick, mystical vapor that envelops the
caster's entire group. As the cloud slowly dissipates, it leaves behind
a residual invisibility effect on all group members present, concealing
them from normal sight.

The spell affects all grouped members in the same room as the caster,
making it far more efficient than casting individual invisibility spells
on each person. The invisibility typically lasts around 12 hours, though
duration may vary based on the caster's skill.

Group members must remain in the room until the cloud dissipates for the
invisibility to take effect. The concealment breaks upon taking offensive
action, as with normal invisibility.

See Also: INVISIBILITY, DISPEL INVISIBLE
